FILED s530b (Opus agent, 2026-10-31), from the Template-Toolkit re-census.  PRE-EXISTING (main 5faf9c8f).  SILENT.

    my $b;
    my $src = { a => sub { "A" }, b => sub { "B" }, c => [1] };
    my $h = { map { $b = $src->{$_}; ($_ => $b) } sort keys %$src };
    print join(",", map { "$_=" . ref($h->{$_}) } sort keys %$h), "\n";   # perl a=CODE,b=CODE,c=ARRAY   PCL a=ARRAY,b=ARRAY,c=ARRAY
    my @l = map { $b = $src->{$_}; $b } qw(a b);
    print join(",", map { $_->() } @l), "\n";                            # perl A,B   PCL B,B
perl: each map iteration's value is COPIED when the list is stored (the hash / array assignment copies its elements).  PCL: the outer `$b` box itself goes into the result -- for a NUMBER or STRING value the copy happens (`map { $b = $_ * 2; ($_ => $b) }` is right, probed), for a REFERENCE value the element keeps the shared box, so every slot reads the last reference.  Probe: scratch/s530b/p/mapalias2.pl (and mapalias.pl: the scalar-value twin, correct).
Likely the same family as #3824 (s529a: a reference copied into a NEW array element is a new container) -- this is the map / anon-hash-constructor path that fix did not reach; check %p-assign-snapshot / the hash constructor's element copy for a ref-holding box.

Template-Toolkit: Template/Context.pm:895-904 builds `$self->{BLOCKS} = { map { $block = $blocks->{$_}; $block = $self->template(\$block) ... unless ref $block; ($_ => $block) } keys %$blocks }` -- every BLOCKS entry (header / footer / block_a / block_b in t/block.t) is the LAST one ("this is block b"): t/block.t rows 9 and 11.
